#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:23
msgid ""
"The B<epoll> API performs a similar task to B<poll>(2): monitoring multiple "
"file descriptors to see if I/O is possible on any of them.  The B<epoll> API "
"can be used either as an edge-triggered or a level-triggered interface and "
"scales well to large numbers of watched file descriptors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:31
msgid ""
"The central concept of the B<epoll> API is the B<epoll> I<instance>, an "
"in-kernel data structure which, from a user-space perspective, can be "
"considered as a container for two lists:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:31 build/C/man7/epoll.7:38 build/C/man7/epoll.7:52
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:61 build/C/man7/epoll.7:67 build/C/man7/epoll.7:359
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:367 build/C/man7/epoll.7:401 build/C/man7/epoll.7:411
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:421 build/C/man7/epoll.7:435 build/C/man7/epoll.7:442
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:481 build/C/man7/epoll.7:487 build/C/man7/epoll.7:495
#: build/C/man7/epoll.7:534 build/C/man7/epoll.7:550
#: build/C/man2/epoll_wait.2:62 build/C/man2/epoll_wait.2:64
#: build/C/man2/epoll_wait.2:67 build/C/man2/poll.2:115 build/C/man2/poll.2:117
#: build/C/man2/poll.2:120 build/C/man2/poll.2:160 build/C/man2/poll.2:163
#: build/C/man2/poll.2:167 build/C/man2/poll.2:465 build/C/man2/poll.2:469
